DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 0, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -6, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, 6, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, -6, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 6, 7>") x Compute("<0, -6, -8>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 0, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 0, -5>") . Compute("<7, 6, 7>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, 5, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, -6, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, -6, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, -6, -1>") . Compute("<-4, 5, -9>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<8, -6, -1>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -1, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 2, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -10, 5, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 5, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 2, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -1, 7>") . Compute("<2, 2, 5>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 5, -8>") x Compute("<2, 2, 5>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 5, -8>") x Compute("<-4, -1, 7>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, -9, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 1, 1, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, 1, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 1, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -9, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, -9, 6>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, 2, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, -6, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -10, -10, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 2, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, -10, 5>") x Compute("<9, -6, -10>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 2, 2>") . Compute("<-10, -10, 5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -6, -10>") x Compute("<-10, -10, 5>")}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
